<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Second Anglo-Burmese War</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1852">1852</a>–<a href="/years/1853">1853</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Second Anglo-Burmese War was fought in 1852–1853 between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> and the Konbaung kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/burma">Burma</a>. Begun by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-india-company">East India Company</a> over a trade dispute in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yangon">Rangoon</a>, it ended with the British annexation of the province of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bago">Pegu</a>, giving Britain all of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lower-burma">Lower Burma</a>. During the war <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mindon-min">Mindon Min</a> deposed his half-brother <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pagan-min">Pagan Min</a> and took the throne.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/second-anglo-burmese-war.jpg" alt="Second Anglo-Burmese War" width="320" height="234" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Royal_Burmese_Troops_(1852).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
